infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title "Email is just CRUD" vs the design that scales to a billion mailboxes
  desc The same four problems — attachments, search, sync, spam — each flip from ruinous to affordable with one design move
  compares
    - label Naive "email is CRUD"
      children
        - label Full attachment copy per recipient
          desc A 2 MB PDF to 50M users writes 50M copies = 100 TB for one send
        - label Scan the mailbox to search
          desc 200K messages scanned per query — can't hit sub-100 ms
        - label Re-list the whole mailbox to sync
          desc O(mailbox): every device re-fetches 200K messages on refresh
        - label Store first, filter spam later
          desc Durably store, index, replicate ~10x the mail you keep
    - label Scaled design
      children
        - label Dedup attachment into object storage
          desc One ref-counted blob + 50M tiny pointers — bytes stored once
        - label Per-user inverted index
          desc Intersect short posting lists — tens of ms over 200K messages
        - label Sync by per-mailbox change log
          desc O(changes): fetch only mutations since your last counter
        - label Reject spam at SMTP ingest
          desc ~90% rejected before storage with cheap IP/auth checks
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
